---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '@components/Section.astro';
import Career from '@components/home/Career.astro';
import Button from '@components/Button.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="From education, into marketing, into operations — the background behind the systems work."
>
  <Section kicker="About" heading="A working practice, not a highlight reel." reveal>
    <div class="max-w-(--container-prose) space-y-6 text-ink-700">
      <p>
        The path here didn't start with operations. It started with running an independent
        education practice for six years — the kind of work where you're responsible for
        everything at once, because there's no one else to hand it to.
      </p>
      <p>
        From there, the work moved into marketing: first as a specialist executing campaigns,
        then managing digital marketing, then leading marketing communications end to end. Three
        roles, three companies, each one a step up in scope — content, lead generation, brand
        visuals, campaign strategy.
      </p>
      <p>
        The shift into operations happened at Perla Engineering — starting in marketing, then
        moving into an operations role once it became clear that the more valuable work was
        further upstream: not just producing content or campaigns, but building the systems that
        let a business actually run — daily reporting, material requests, a defined operating
        rhythm for the role itself.
      </p>
      <p>
        That practice is now continuing at Tathmeer Properties, consolidating reporting across a
        larger project portfolio. Alongside it, three books have been written over the past
        decade — on time, on balance, and on self-coaching — a separate but related thread about
        how people (not just businesses) actually get better at their work.
      </p>
      <p>
        The throughline across all of it: understand how something actually works, find where
        it's breaking, and build the smallest system that fixes it. Not a title, not a pitch —
        just the way the work has consistently gone.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Career />

  <Section tone="dim" reveal>
    <div class="flex flex-col items-start gap-6 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
      <p class="max-w-md text-ink-700">
        A fuller professional profile — experience, results, skills, education — is on the CV
        page.
      </p>
      <Button href="/cv" variant="secondary" arrow>View the CV</Button>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
